('deity.chinese.gonggong','Gonggong','共工','共工','Gònggōng','DEITY','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Figure who contends with Zhuanxu and strikes Mount Buzhou in the Huainanzi Tian Wen and Liezi Tang Wen witnesses; whether deity, clan head or rival ruler is foregrounded varies by source and is not resolved here.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"designations":["共工","共工氏"]}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('hero.chinese.zhuanxu','Zhuanxu','颛顼','顓頊','Zhuānxū','HERO','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Legendary sovereign named as the rival of Gonggong in the Huainanzi and Liezi witnesses; no historical-reality claim is made.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"reality":"LEGENDARY_SOVEREIGN"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('place.chinese.buzhou_mountain','Mount Buzhou','不周山','不周之山','Bùzhōu zhī shān','MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Mountain struck by Gonggong in the Huainanzi Tian Wen and Liezi Tang Wen witnesses; not mapped to any modern mountain.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"reality":"MYTHICAL","coordinate_policy":"NO_COORDINATE"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('creature.chinese.ao_turtle','Ao (great turtle)','鳌','鼇','áo','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Great turtle whose legs Nüwa cuts to set up the four poles in the Huainanzi Lan Ming and Liezi Tang Wen witnesses.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"glyph_variants":["鼇","鰲"]}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('dragon.chinese.black_dragon_jizhou','Black dragon of the Nüwa passage','黑龙（女娲补天段）','黑龍','hēilóng','DRAGON','civ.chinese_ancient','Western Han textual witness','Black dragon killed by Nüwa to relieve Jizhou in the Huainanzi Lan Ming witness; not stated in the Liezi Tang Wen witness.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witness_scope":"Huainanzi Lan Ming only"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('artifact.chinese.five_colored_stones','Five-colored stones','五色石','五色石','wǔsè shí','SACRED_OBJECT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Stones that Nüwa refines to repair the sky in both the Huainanzi Lan Ming and Liezi Tang Wen witnesses; glyph variants of the refining verb occur across received editions.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('event.chinese.nuwa_repairs_sky','Nüwa repairs the sky','女娲补天','女媧補天','Nǚwā bǔ tiān','EVENT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Narrative event registered separately from the Huainanzi Lan Ming and Liezi Tang Wen witnesses; later causal retellings are not merged into either witness.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witnesses":2}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('event.chinese.gonggong_strikes_buzhou','Gonggong strikes Mount Buzhou','共工触不周山','共工觸不周之山','Gònggōng chù Bùzhōu zhī shān','EVENT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Etiological narrative event for the tilt of heaven and earth attested in Huainanzi Tian Wen and Liezi Tang Wen; neither registered witness makes it the cause of Nüwa''s repair.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witnesses":2}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.chinese.liezi','Liezi','列子','列子','Lièzǐ','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received text; compilation date debated','Compendium attributed to Lie Yukou; the date of the received compilation is debated.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.chinese.huainanzi.lanming_nuwa_passage','Huainanzi Lan Ming Nüwa passage witness','《淮南子·览冥训》女娲段落见证','覽冥訓「往古之時」段','Lǎnmíng xùn','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Western Han','Scoped passage witness in Lan Ming Xun describing cosmic collapse and Nüwa''s repair.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"chapter":"覽冥訓"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.chinese.huainanzi.tianwen_gonggong_passage','Huainanzi Tian Wen Gonggong passage witness','《淮南子·天文训》共工段落见证','天文訓「昔者共工」段','Tiānwén xùn','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Western Han','Scoped passage witness in Tian Wen Xun narrating Gonggong striking Mount Buzhou as a cosmological etiology.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"chapter":"天文訓"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.chinese.liezi.tangwen_nuwa_gonggong_passage','Liezi Tang Wen Nüwa–Gonggong passage witness','《列子·汤问》女娲—共工段落见证','湯問「天地亦物」段','Tāngwèn','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received Liezi; compilation date debated','Scoped passage witness in which Nüwa''s repair is followed by the Gonggong episode.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"chapter":"湯問"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('event.hindu.samudra_manthana','Churning of the Ocean (textual narrative)','乳海搅拌（文本叙事）','समुद्रमन्थन','samudramanthana','EVENT','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Textual narrative event registered from separate Mahābhārata critical-edition and Bhāgavata Purāṇa witnesses; kept distinct from the Angkor Wat material-witness scene.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witnesses":2}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('place.hindu.mandara','Mount Mandara','曼陀罗山','मन्दर','Mandara','MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Mountain used as the churning rod in both registered textual witnesses; not mapped to any modern hill.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"reality":"MYTHICAL","coordinate_policy":"NO_COORDINATE"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('creature.hindu.vasuki','Vāsuki','婆苏吉','वासुकि','Vāsuki','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Nāga king used as the churning rope in both registered textual witnesses.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('creature.hindu.akupara','Akūpāra, king of tortoises','龟王阿库帕拉','अकूपार','Akūpāra','DIVINE_BEAST','civ.hindu','Mahābhārata critical-edition layer','Tortoise king who bears Mount Mandara in the Mahābhārata critical-edition witness; that witness does not identify him with a form of Viṣṇu.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witness_scope":"Mahābhārata CE 1.16"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.kurma','Kūrma','俱利摩（龟形化身）','कूर्म','Kūrma','DEITY','civ.hindu','Bhāgavata Purāṇa layer','Tortoise form assumed by Viṣṇu to support Mount Mandara in the Bhāgavata Purāṇa witness; kept separate from the Mahābhārata tortoise king Akūpāra.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witness_scope":"Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.7"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.mohini','Mohinī','摩希尼','मोहिनी','Mohinī','DEITY','civ.hindu','Bhāgavata Purāṇa layer','Enchanting female form of Viṣṇu who distributes the amṛta in the Bhāgavata Purāṇa witness; the Mahābhārata witness is linked only through its own description of a deluding female form.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"witness_scope":"Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.8–8.9"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.dhanvantari','Dhanvantari','檀文陀利','धन्वन्तरि','Dhanvantari','DEITY','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Divine figure who emerges from the churned ocean carrying the amṛta in both registered textual witnesses.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('artifact.hindu.amrita','Amṛta','甘露（阿姆利塔）','अमृत','amṛta','SACRED_OBJECT','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Nectar of immortality sought through the churning in both registered textual witnesses.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('demon.hindu.rahu','Rāhu','罗睺','राहु','Rāhu','DEMON','civ.hindu','Epic and Purāṇic narrative layers','Dānava who drinks the amṛta in disguise and is beheaded with Viṣṇu''s discus in both registered textual witnesses.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.indian.mahabharata.adiparvan_churning','Mahābhārata critical-edition Ādiparvan 1.15–1.17 churning witness','《摩诃婆罗多》精校本初篇 1.15–1.17 搅海见证','आदिपर्वन् १.१५–१.१७','Ādiparvan 1.15–1.17','TEXT','civ.hindu','Layered epic composition; critical edition 1933','Scoped passage witness in the constituted text of the BORI critical edition (Āstīkaparvan).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"edition":"BORI critical edition"}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.hindu.bhagavata_purana','Bhāgavata Purāṇa','薄伽梵往世书','भागवतपुराण','Bhāgavatapurāṇa','SCRIPTURE','civ.hindu','Purāṇic layer; scholarly dating varies','Purāṇa in twelve skandhas that remains scripture in living devotional traditions.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z'),
('text.hindu.bhagavata_purana.skandha8_churning','Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.5–8.9 churning witness','《薄伽梵往世书》第八篇第5–9章搅海见证','भागवतपुराण ८.५–८.९','Bhāgavatapurāṇa 8.5–8.9','TEXT','civ.hindu','Purāṇic layer; scholarly dating varies','Scoped passage witness for the churning sequence in Skandha 8.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"skandha":8}','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z','2026-10-02T05:40:00Z');

